  ],
  "cues": [
    {
      "start": 0,
      "end": 3.5999999046325684,
      "text": "Start with the chloroplast schematic, and follow each leader line to its",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 3.5999999046325684,
      "end": 5.320000171661377,
      "text": "endpoint before naming a structure.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 6,
      "end": 10.100000381469727,
      "text": "Label A brackets a stack of flattened sacs: one stack is a granum.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 10.739999771118164,
      "end": 13.4399995803833,
      "text": "B points to a membrane of one sac, a thylakoid.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 13.979999542236328,
      "end": 17.360000610351562,
      "text": "C marks the surrounding internal fluid region, the stroma.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 17.899999618530273,
      "end": 21.65999984741211,
      "text": "D indicates the chloroplast envelope, shown as two boundary lines.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 22.18000030517578,
      "end": 25.959999084472656,
      "text": "The drawing is not to scale and omits many molecular details.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 26.5,
      "end": 30.799999237060547,
      "text": "A bracket around several sacs does not mean one thylakoid, and the stroma is",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 30.799999237060547,
      "end": 32.36000061035156,
      "text": "not the space inside a thylakoid.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 32.36000061035156,
      "end": 32.76000000000035,
      "text": "Pause and explain all four labels without using the answer options.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 32.76000000000035,
      "end": 36.65230777667154,
      "text": "Keep the same chloroplast diagram and turn the labels into functional",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 36.65230777667154,
      "end": 37.160000095367785,
      "text": "evidence.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 38.220000038147326,
      "end": 42.100000152588244,
      "text": "Light dependent electron transport occurs on the thylakoid membrane indicated",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 42.100000152588244,
      "end": 42.6800000762943,
      "text": "by B.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 43.49999977111852,
      "end": 47.100000152588244,
      "text": "Calvin cycle reactions occur in the stroma indicated by C.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 47.95999980926549,
      "end": 53.23999954223668,
      "text": "ATP and NADPH from the light reactions support carbon reduction, but a",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 53.23999954223668,
      "end": 56.571795699291094,
      "text": "structure drawing alone does not tell you the actual rate in a particular",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 56.571795699291094,
      "end": 56.8000009155277,
      "text": "leaf.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 57.49999977111852,
      "end": 61.26000000000035,
      "text": "The double envelope at D is a separate membrane system from the thylakoids.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 61.88000083923375,
      "end": 66.71999908447302,
      "text": "If a question swaps the words stroma and granum, test the location rather than",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 66.71999908447302,
      "end": 67.50000167846716,
      "text": "memorising the letter.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 68.48000122070349,
      "end": 71.82000137329138,
      "text": "Letters are local to this schematic and can be reassigned in another question.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 72.12000000000096,
      "end": 76.46000015258885,
      "text": "Read the circulation diagram as a connectivity map rather than an anatomical",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 76.46000015258885,
      "end": 76.88000022888279,
      "text": "portrait.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 77.52000009536839,
      "end": 83.4799996566782,
      "text": "The arrows run from body to A, then B, then lungs, then C, then D and back to",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 83.4799996566782,
      "end": 83.72000038147068,
      "text": "body.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 84.35999977111912,
      "end": 89.17999946594334,
      "text": "In the standard adult human circulation, A is the right atrium and B the right",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 89.17999946594334,
      "end": 89.56000053405857,
      "text": "ventricle.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 90.22000038147068,
      "end": 93.22000038147068,
      "text": "C is the left atrium and D the left ventricle.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 93.57999908447361,
      "end": 97.4199992370615,
      "text": "A and C are receiving chambers; B and D pump blood out of the heart.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 97.90000068664646,
      "end": 101.32000076294041,
      "text": "Their positions on the screen do not establish anatomical left and right.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 101.98000061035252,
      "end": 104.07999908447361,
      "text": "Follow where blood comes from and where it goes.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 104.70000183105564,
      "end": 109.08000000000146,
      "text": "This diagram deliberately prioritises the route over realistic chamber shapes.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 109.08000000000146,
      "end": 112.33999999046472,
      "text": "Use the same route to avoid a common naming error.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 113.40000017166284,
      "end": 117.42886105453059,
      "text": "An artery carries blood away from the heart; a vein carries it toward the",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 117.42886105453059,
      "end": 117.76000030517724,
      "text": "heart.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 118.76000030517724,
      "end": 120.58000000000146,
      "text": "Oxygen content is not the definition.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 121.42000015258935,
      "end": 125.47999961853174,
      "text": "In the standard adult pulmonary circuit, the artery leaving B carries",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 125.47999961853174,
      "end": 130.53999908447412,
      "text": "relatively deoxygenated blood toward the lungs, while pulmonary veins return",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 130.53999908447412,
      "end": 132.36000068664697,
      "text": "oxygenated blood to C.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 133.10000045776513,
      "end": 134.97999961853174,
      "text": "D pumps into the systemic circuit.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 135.45000083923486,
      "end": 139.1693597480593,
      "text": "The arrows show connectivity and direction, not a measured pressure",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 139.1693597480593,
      "end": 139.78000076294092,
      "text": "difference,",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 140.42000015258935,
      "end": 141.98000152588037,
      "text": "blood speed or cardiac output.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 142.78000076294092,
      "end": 146.48000152588037,
      "text": "If a question asks for one of those quantities, it must provide additional",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 146.48000152588037,
      "end": 147.0599995422378,
      "text": "information.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 148.14000137329248,
      "end": 152.53999908447412,
      "text": "First identify the chamber and circuit, then classify the vessel by its",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 152.53999908447412,
      "end": 154.08000000000146,
      "text": "direction relative to the heart.",
      "chapter": 3
    },
    {
      "start": 154.3440000000023,
      "end": 156.48400010490647,
      "text": "Now read the embryo sac schematic.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 157.3440000000023,
      "end": 161.44399990463486,
      "text": "The chalazal end is at the top and the micropylar end at the bottom.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 162.38399996185532,
      "end": 165.52400030517808,
      "text": "A identifies the three antipodal cells at the chalazal end.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 166.3440000000023,
      "end": 171.54400076294175,
      "text": "C points to the egg at the micropylar end, and D identifies the two flanking",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 171.54400076294175,
      "end": 172.14399923706284,
      "text": "synergids.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 172.94400038147202,
      "end": 176.10400022888413,
      "text": "B marks the two polar nuclei in the large central cell.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 176.64399923706284,
      "end": 179.54400076294175,
      "text": "The egg and synergids together form the egg apparatus.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 180.48399938965073,
      "end": 184.52400030517808,
      "text": "Do not decide the identity from top and bottom alone, because another drawing",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 184.52400030517808,
      "end": 185.30399908447495,
      "text": "may be rotated.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 186.08399977112046,
      "end": 190.72400106811753,
      "text": "This figure specifies the common Polygonum type pattern before polar nuclear",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 190.72400106811753,
      "end": 195.4040013732933,
      "text": "fusion; it is not a claim that every flowering plant has exactly this",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 195.4040013732933,
      "end": 195.70400061035386,
      "text": "arrangement.",
      "chapter": 4
    },
    {
      "start": 196.296000000003,
      "end": 201.4159998855621,
      "text": "Count the six small cells in the drawing: three antipodals, two synergids and",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 201.4159998855621,
      "end": 201.83599996185603,
      "text": "one egg.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 202.53599977112117,
      "end": 205.21600007629695,
      "text": "Add the large central cell to obtain seven cells.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 205.95599984741511,
      "end": 210.41087185649684,
      "text": "Before polar nuclear fusion, the central cell contains two nuclei, so the",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 210.41087185649684,
      "end": 210.71600007629695,
      "text": "total",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 210.71600007629695,
      "end": 211.71600007629695,
      "text": "is eight nuclei.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 212.5159993133575,
      "end": 217.1360001525909,
      "text": "During normal double fertilisation, one sperm fuses with the egg at C to form",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 217.1360001525909,
      "end": 218.1360001525909,
      "text": "the diploid zygote.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 218.6360001525909,
      "end": 222.95599984741511,
      "text": "The other combines with the two haploid polar nuclei at B, or their already",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 222.95599984741511,
      "end": 227.19599961853328,
      "text": "fused secondary nucleus, to form the typical triploid primary endosperm",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 227.19599961853328,
      "end": 227.6360001525909,
      "text": "nucleus.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 228.49600076294246,
      "end": 231.8959984741241,
      "text": "Count cells separately from nuclei, and state the developmental stage.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 232.4760003051788,
      "end": 236.6360001525909,
      "text": "A change in nuclear fusion does not automatically imply another cell division.",
      "chapter": 5
    },
    {
      "start": 236.90400000000366,
      "end": 242.8240000762976,
      "text": "The final schematic shows grass at A, grasshopper at B, frog at C and snake",
      "chapter": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 242.8240000762976,
      "end": 243.40400000000366,
      "text": "at D.",
      "chapter": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 244.14399977112183,
      "end": 247.14399977112183,
      "text": "Read the arrows as energy transfer from food to consumer.",
      "chapter": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 247.80399961853394,
      "end": 253.12399931335815,
      "text": "A is the producer, B the primary consumer, C the secondary consumer and D",
      "chapter": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 253.12399931335815,
      "end": 255.80399961853394,
      "text": "the tertiary consumer in this stated grazing chain.",
      "chapter": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 256.16400022888547,
      "end": 260.8639990844763,
      "text": "The drawing is a simplified model: real diets can form food webs, and",
      "chapter": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 260.8639990844763,
      "end": 263.40400000000363,
      "text": "decomposers participate even though they are not drawn.",
      "chapter": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 263.8639990844763,
      "end": 267.8639990844763,
      "text": "Do not interpret a missing box as proof that a process does not occur in",
      "chapter": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 267.8639990844763,
      "end": 268.02400083923703,
      "text": "nature.",
      "chapter": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 268.944000915531,
      "end": 272.7640006103552,
      "text": "Identify the trophic level from the given feeding relationship, not just the",
      "chapter": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 272.7640006103552,
      "end": 273.944000915531,
      "text": "animal's name in isolation.",
      "chapter": 6
    },
    {
      "start": 274.2720000000042,
      "end": 278.71200005722466,
      "text": "For this calculation only, apply ten percent transfer at each boundary.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 279.71200005722466,
      "end": 284.02661566754296,
      "text": "Starting with ten thousand kilojoules at A gives one thousand at B, one",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 284.02661566754296,
      "end": 284.45200030518,
      "text": "hundred",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 284.45200030518,
      "end": 286.2720000000042,
      "text": "at C and ten at D.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 286.7119995803875,
      "end": 291.3720003814739,
      "text": "There are three transfers between A and D, so multiply by zero point one three",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 291.3720003814739,
      "end": 291.9319998474163,
      "text": "times.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 292.67199961853447,
      "end": 296.51199977112236,
      "text": "If you compare production measurements, they must refer to matching areas and",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 296.51199977112236,
      "end": 297.13200061035576,
      "text": "time periods.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 297.95200030518,
      "end": 301.95200030518,
      "text": "Ten percent is a stated teaching approximation, not an exact measured",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 301.95200030518,
      "end": 303.47200076294365,
      "text": "efficiency for every ecosystem.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 304.1120001525921,
      "end": 308.07199923706474,
      "text": "The energy not incorporated into the next level's production follows other",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 308.07199923706474,
      "end": 312.012001678471,
      "text": "pathways, including respiration, waste and uneaten material.",
      "chapter": 7
    },
    {
      "start": 312.7519995422405,
      "end": 315.3719984741253,
      "text": "It is not all stored as biomass in the next box.",
      "chapter": 7
    }
  ]
}
